  "script": [
    "These pills made baby mice into dwarfs. Not clickbait: dwarfism is the actual word in the paper.",
    "Ibuprofen, aspirin, naproxen all block COX, the enzyme that makes prostaglandins. And prostaglandins help growth plates turn cartilage into bone.",
    "In twenty fifteen, blocking COX slowed growth plate cell division. Add prostaglandins back, and it recovers. Inject these drugs into young mice: dwarfism.",
    "More receipts. Rat cells dying in a dish. Cartilage struggling to mature. Rabbits with slower bone mineralisation. Growing mice on naproxen with shorter leg bones.",
    "My take? These are animal studies with long daily dosing. A short, normal course probably won't shrink you. Plot twist: flurbiprofen, also an NSAID, boosted bone growth in young rats."
  ],
